 extremely hopeful  that uh  come july the 19th we will be able to  move step four and  everybody will be able to go back to the  theater hanya you were going to say the  delta variant so i looked up the figures  125 reported deaths uh the  week ending the 11th of june the lowest  in eight months and certainly that does  take into account  uh the delta variance so again i put it  to you  the nightclub industry at the theater  industry  so the festival industry is on its knees  they need to see this report  you have it and you won't show it to  them  we will share it to them we've said we  will publish the report we've always  been clear  we will publish the report before we  move to step four we will demonstrate to  people  the evidence and the analysis of the  results of the programme  and the basis on which we have reached a  conclusion that it is i very much hope  safe to move to step four and you know  we have been through  a horrendous year or more now um the  last thing we want to do is throw away  the success we've had  it's only another couple of weeks the  chancellor has provided  okay okay okay uh okay we've got it  we've got it  19th of july you're going to publish the  report before then yeah  yes we've said we will publish it before  we reach decision on step four okay fine  uh talk to me about holiday uh  destinations uh where are where are we  as far as that is concerned looking at  the figures  our figures in the uk are much worse  than most of mainland europe and uh  malta um are we expecting several  european countries to go onto the green  list later on in the week  well we've said that we will be looking  later in the week  to make revisions to the green list and  i hope that we can put more countries  onto it you know i quite understand why  people  want to go on their summer holidays i  would say to them that you can have a  great whole day in britain and i think a  very large number of  people will decide this year that that's  what they will 